 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "spec_point",
   "id": "spcpt_KNXbNby67zKvX8SX",
   "name": "Ordering FDP",
   "definition": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Ordering FDP"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I put fractions in order of size?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- When comparing **only fractions**, write them over a **lowest common denominator**\n\n  - For $\\frac{3}{5},\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{13}{20},\\frac{7}{12}$, the lowest common denominator is **60**\n  - So change them to $\\frac{36}{60},\\frac{30}{60},\\frac{39}{60},\\frac{35}{60}$ and then** order them by their numerators**\n  - From smallest to largest: $\\frac{30}{60},\\frac{35}{60},\\frac{36}{60},\\frac{39}{60}$\n  - Rewrite in their original form: $\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{7}{12},\\frac{3}{5},\\frac{13}{20}$\n- Alternatively, a **calculator **can be used to **convert each fraction to a decimal**\n\n  - To do this, enter each fraction as a division"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "How do I put fractions, decimals and percentages in order of size?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- When comparing a mixture of fractions, decimals and percentages, **change everything into decimals**"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2026/01/24271-ordering-fractions-decimals-and-percentages-1.png",
   "file": "assets/935d93187168-24271-ordering-fractions-decimals-and-percentage.png",
   "alt": "Ordering fractions, decimals, and percentages",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2026/01/48832-ordering-fractions-decimals-and-percentages-2.png",
   "file": "assets/c53c30574455-48832-ordering-fractions-decimals-and-percentage.png",
   "alt": "Order by Size Notes fig5 (2)",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2026/01/9026-ordering-fractions-decimals-and-percentages-3.png",
   "file": "assets/eb0ae508109a-9026-ordering-fractions-decimals-and-percentages.png",
   "alt": "Order by Size Notes fig5 (3)",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Which symbols can I use?"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- Rather than just listing values in order, symbols can be used to compare them\n\n  - For example, $\\frac{1}{4}<\\frac{1}{3}<\\frac{1}{2}$\n- Recall that $>$ means **greater than** and $\\geq$ means greater than **or equal to**\n\n  - Similarly, $<$ means **less **than and $\\leq$ means less than or equal to\n- You may also see $=$and $\\neq$ (which means \"**not **equal to\")"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "exam-tip",
   "label": "Exam Hint",
   "md": "A calculator can be used to quickly convert any quantities into decimals.\n\nE.g. A fraction can be entered as a division."
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "worked-example",
   "label": "Worked Example",
   "md": "Without use of a calculator, write these numbers in order, starting with the smallest.\n\n$\\frac{1}{3}$,       $\\frac{2}{5}$,     $\\frac{9}{25}$,      $\\frac{4}{15}$\n\n**Answer:**\n\n> *As they are all fractions, write them with a common denominator*\n*The lowest common denominator is 75*\n*Rewrite each fraction with a denominator of 75*\n\n* *$\\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{25}{75}$*                       *$\\frac{2}{5}=\\frac{30}{75}$*                      *$\\frac{9}{25}=\\frac{27}{75}$*                 *$\\frac{4}{15}=\\frac{20}{75}$*            *\n\n> *Compare and write in order from smallest to largest*\n\n$\\frac{20}{75},\\frac{25}{75},\\frac{27}{75},\\frac{30}{75}$\n\n> *Rewrite in their original form*\n\n$\\frac{4}{15},\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{9}{25},\\frac{2}{5}$"
  },
  {
   "type": "callout",
   "variant": "worked-example",
   "label": "Worked Example",
   "md": "Write these numbers in the spaces below.\n\n$\\frac{7}{8}$,       $\\frac{5}{6}$,       $0.8$,       `78 percent sign`\n\n..... < ..... < ..... < .....\n\n**Answer:**\n\n> *As there is a mixture of fractions, decimals, and percentages, rewrite each as a decimal*\n\n> *0.8 is already a decimal*\n\n> *Convert 78% to a decimal by dividing by 100*\n\n`78 percent sign space equals space 0.78`\n\n> *Convert *$\\frac{7}{8}$* to a decimal by entering into a calculator as a division*\n\n$\\frac{7}{8}=7\\div8=0.875$\n\n> *Convert *$\\frac{5}{6}$* to a decimal in the same way*\n\n`5 over 6 equals 5 divided by 6 equals 0.8333... equals 0.8 3 with dot on top`\n\n> *Write them all with 3 decimal places to determine the order*\n\n$0.875\\,0.833\\,0.800\\,0.780$\n\n> *Rewrite the decimals in order*\n\n`0.78 comma space 0.8 comma space 0.8 3 with dot on top comma space 0.875`\n\n> *Rewrite in their original form, and recall that < means \"less than\", so the smallest value will be first*\n\n`bold 78 bold percent sign bold space bold less than bold space bold 0 bold. bold 8 bold space bold less than bold space bold 5 over bold 6 bold space bold less than bold space bold 7 over bold 8`"
  }
 ]
}